I wake up every mornin'

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.920
Entspresso keep me goin'

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:23.540
You know, and the first job I got was, a real job besides commercials and things like that

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:27.560
local radio commercials and things that kind of gave us the money

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.660
Ben and I had a joint bank account and we'd go to New York

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:33.200
And if you had made money acting, it went into the account

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:38.120
And the account was to be used if you were going to New York for an audition

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:41.960
Or if we took ten dollars out to like play video games, okay? (laugh out loud) and uh

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:47.120
I got a line in the movie 'Mystic Pizza' and the line was "Mom do you want my green stuff?" and literally

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:52.880
But it was a scene that was a big dinner table scene. Julia Roberts, it was like a big movie for her

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:58.000
And uh it was this whole dinner table scene, and so it took us three nights to shoot

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.200
down in Mystic, Connecticut. And I was a minor so my mother had to come with me

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:06.600
And, you know, we shot from five to five every night

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:14.120
And uh and, I just remember being so in love with the process of filming

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:18.940
I just knew, I was like this is the greatest, it was the best time I'd ever had in my life

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:23.980
And it was, you know, I was like this is amazing. I want this to never ever ever stop

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:24.940
Like I loved it

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:28.420
So this is the message that's been repeated over and over and over again on the channel

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:35.880
From actors to musicians, to entrepreneurs, to investors, to politicians, to athletes, to like all over the place

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:39.460
The people who are at the top of there field love what they do

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:44.020
And it feels like it's another video saying the same thing

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:48.380
But it's just so important. And I feel like so many people are not doing what they love

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:52.480
So many people are doing the things that they feel like they have to do, or that just pays the bills

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:58.360
And they've shut off that part of themselves where they really enjoy the work that they're doing

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:01.740
And not everyday is gonna be amazing, and not every task you do is gonna be awesome

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.180
But net net that's gotta be enough of what you're doing on a daily basis that you love

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:09.500
If you're gonna have any kind of real success in this world

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:15.140
And I encourage you to explore until you find the thing that you just can't stop doing

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.660
You know, for Matt Damon, it was doing acting

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:22.980
For me, I remember doing a speech helping some young entrepreneurs out of the YMCA

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:25.700
And you know, only three people showed up, and I've told this story a number of times

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:31.000
But, I just felt so good. I can get lost in having discussions with entrepreneurs

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:37.720
And it just is so rewarding and amazing and fulfilling and for me as someone who's an introvert, believe it or not

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:41.500
who doesn't need to be surrounded by people, who needs to have time by himself

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:47.440
but if I find out that you are an entrepreneur, I am hooked. And I wanna help you

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:50.500
And I wanna get you where you wanna go, and I wanna know what your dream is

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:54.340
And I wanna know what impact you wanna have. I just get so fired up

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:59.560
It's a thing that makes me come alive the most. And I'm so grateful that I've discovered that

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:03.400
And I encourage you to go out and find that for yourself if you haven't already

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.640
Or if you have before and you've lost some interest in it

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:11.640
then, what's the pivot, what's the change? So that the work that you're doing isn't just okay

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:15.400
but it's great! And you're working on something that's really inspiring you

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.980
and really pushing you to be better

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.900
I think people just settle too much

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:22.580
I think people just don't make their highest aspirations important enough

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:26.080
And so you settle for good, and you have a good life

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:31.560
And you know, the goals you have are okay, and if you don't reach them, you know, whatever

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.420
And you just settle too much

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:35.880
Where when you find something that you truly love

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:39.560
You will push yourself beyond what you thought was possible

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:42.500
to create something no one even imagined before

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:49.360
And that is exciting. And I deeply, truly, hopefully, uh, want that for you as well

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:57.660
So the question to date today is 'What is it that you love the most doing? What is it that you can get lost in

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:00.640
And just feel the love of the work

